disclaude.md:5207:## §11 HEARTBEAT — REL-RC-E design (bad_range→STUCK loop-recovery gap) — Explore-mapped
disclaude.md:5213:**REL-RC-E fix (Codex plan-gating):**
disclaude.md:5219:## §11 HEARTBEAT — REL-RC-E IMPLEMENTED + Codex CODE-gate APPROVE (A+B; C dropped)
disclaude.md:5227:NEXT (do NOT restart mid-soak): when soak-rcd3 finishes → restart stack (deploy REL-RC-E) → REL-RC-E verification soak revise_thrice ×5, then a 2nd ×5. ALSO investigate: WORKSPACE_SNAPSHOT_NOT_READY recurring even at 45s snapshot-wait (agent final-bytes sha != flushed disk sha within 45s) — harness-measurement INVALID, root-cause whether snapshot flush is genuinely slow or the oracle's sha expectation races the agent's last write.
disclaude.md:5231:Explore-mapped (definitive): NOT a product snapshot-flush race (the product snapshot faithfully holds the agent's true final bytes; raising 15→45s had no effect because on-disk is already stable-and-correct). It's a HARNESS expected-sha derivation bug: build_soak _agent_declared_expected (disco_api.py:1559-1643) reconstructs each declared file's FINAL sha from the event log using an INCOMPLETE tool model — _FILE_WRITE_FULL_TOOLS={file_write} and _FILE_WRITE_PARTIAL_TOOLS omitted exact_replace + safe_write_file. In revise_thrice the model is steered to exact_replace for targeted follow-up edits (files.py:1345); when a revision's FINAL touch is exact_replace/safe_write_file, that op is invisible → 'expected' pins to an EARLIER file_write sha → permanent mismatch vs the correct latest snapshot bytes → false WORKSPACE_SNAPSHOT_NOT_READY (fatal 'sha' class, disco_api.py:1067). FIX (committed): safe_write_file→FULL (writes args.content verbatim → sha-precise), exact_replace→PARTIAL (→present_unproven, accepted best-effort). Verified end-to-end by the re-soak (no unit-test scaffold exists for this internal fn; the soak is the honest proof).
disclaude.md:5233:Three harness robustness fixes now: HttpTransport 30→120s (cold-start ReadTimeout), snapshot-wait 15→45s (flush headroom), expected-sha tool model (this). soak-rcd3 (pre-REL-RC-E) = 3 PASS + 1 false-INVALID(this bug) + 1 running; REL-RC-D holds (0 bad_range, 0 executor-killed; 11 STALE_FILE_CONTEXT all inside PASSING runs = recoverable line-edit re-reads).
disclaude.md:5235:NEXT: soak-rcd3 finishes → restart (deploy REL-RC-E) → REL-RC-E verification soak (now also free of the false snapshot INVALIDs). Expect materially cleaner PASS rate.
disclaude.md:5237:## §11 HEARTBEAT — REL-RC-F found: revision_no_concrete_steps STUCK (actionless revision plan)
disclaude.md:5239:REL-RC-E verification soak (soak-rce, all fixes deployed): iter 000 PASS (+ snapshot fix CONFIRMED via present_unproven acceptance, 0 false INVALID), iter 001 FAIL/STUCK detail=**revision_no_concrete_steps**. NOT bad_range, NOT STALE — a NEW distinct mode. On follow-up 2 ("change every CTA button to Get Started") MiniMax explored (repeated file_read+think = actionless stall, the known dominant real-build failure) then submitted a ZERO-STEP revision plan; engine force-submitted once (engine.py:922-943) and on the still-empty plan emitted the DELIBERATE controlled terminal STUCK(revision_no_concrete_steps) (engine.py:944-952, from prior fix REL-RC A1: never fake-approve an empty revision plan, never strand execution).
disclaude.md:5241:This is OUR engine's recovery gap (never the model): a simple one-file text revision the model can't articulate as formal plan steps → STUCK instead of just executing the edit. Explore agent (aabc89165925d66d6) mapping fix options: (A) improve _FORCE_SUBMIT_DIRECTIVE wording, (B) synthesize ONE implicit step from the follow-up msg + proceed to execution with a minimal tracker (vs STUCK), (C) let a trivial single-file revision skip PLANNING. Lowest-risk likely (B) — aligns with REL-RC A1 intent (no fake approval, no stranded exec) but recovers instead of terminating. Codex plan-gate before implementing.
